!!! archon/rules/catalog.mat
!!! The rule catalog: which rules apply to which kind of target.
!!!
!!! Generic rules apply to every target. Language-specific rule sets are added
!!! when the target's kind matches. The catalog is the single place that decides
!!! this, so a new analyzer changes one function, not every scan site.

book archon.rules.catalog

read everything from ny.lang.core
read everything from archon.model.rule
read everything from archon.rules.generic
read everything from archon.rules.matrix

!!! The rules that apply to a target of the given kind.
public rules-for receives kind as text returns array of knowledge-rule begin paragraph
    variable rules as array of knowledge-rule is generic-rules with nothing

    when kind equals "matrix" then
        value specific is matrix-rules with nothing
        repeat for each rule in specific
            append rule to rules
        end repeat
    end when

    give rules
end paragraph

!!! How many rules apply to a target of the given kind.
public rule-count-for receives kind as text returns number begin paragraph
    give the length of (rules-for with kind being kind)
end paragraph
